            "steps_image_width": 320,
            "step_1_title": "Trace your foot",
            "step_1_text": "<p>Place a sheet of paper on the floor and stand on it while wearing the socks you would normally wear with your shoes. Keep your weight evenly distributed and trace the outline of your foot with a pencil.</p>",
            "step_1_image": "shopify://shop_images/2.png",
            "step_2_title": "Measure foot length",
            "step_2_text": "<p>Mark the heel and the tip of the longest toe, then measure the distance between those two points with a ruler or measuring tape.</p>",
            "step_2_image": "shopify://shop_images/3.png",
            "step_3_title": "Measure ball girth",
            "step_3_text": "<p>Wrap a measuring tape around the widest part of the forefoot (the ball of the foot). Keep the tape snug but not tight, then record the measurement.</p>",
            "step_3_image": "shopify://shop_images/1_d9b0ad8e-6f88-4afc-bac1-85ace846eb3c.png",
            "step_4_title": "Find your size",
            "step_4_text": "<p>Match both your foot length and ball girth to the closest row in the size tables. If you are between two sizes, choose the larger size or contact ADORSI for sizing guidance.</p>",
